From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: allow sampling pooled capture textures

Upstream: https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope/pull/2164
Adapted to 3.16.23.4's shared screenshot/capture texture pool. The RGB-to-NV12
shader samples these images, so their Vulkan usage must include SAMPLED_BIT.

diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -3625,6 +3625,7 @@ static gamescope::Rc<CVulkanTexture> acquire_pooled_texture( auto& pool, uint32
 			textureFlags.bMappable = true;
 			textureFlags.bTransferDst = true;
 			textureFlags.bStorage = true;
+			textureFlags.bSampled = true;
 			if (exportable || drmFormat == DRM_FORMAT_NV12) {
 				textureFlags.bExportable = true;
 				textureFlags.bLinear = true; // TODO: support multi-planar DMA-BUF export via PipeWire
